From 2a8d00b3e4e60b63beb7b76d019626ce7184833c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Carpio <jcarpio@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:27:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Home: Today & Tonight and Today's episodes as vertical
 timelines
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Both Home cards take Entertainment's On screen format.

Today & Tonight keeps its day-part headings ("This afternoon", "Tonight"),
each over Sports' Upcoming timeline (spf-timeline): a rail with a dot in
the sport's color, the time to the left, the matchup in bold and
"Sport · TV" under it. The network moves from its own right-hand column
into that line; a stream stays a link with its play mark. Every row
keeps its time, because "My teams only" hides rows in the browser and a
blanked repeat could lose its only shown time. The five-row limit, the
"N more today" link and team filtering are unchanged (same data
attributes). Venue is dropped; it was already hidden from 744px.

Today's episodes uses the On screen markup (ef-onscreen): one row per
episode in time order, confirmed times first, the time shown once per
slot, a 34x50 poster beside the series title and "TV · network · S01 E02
· title" under it. Unconfirmed times read "TBA" (screen readers: "Time
not confirmed").

Removed the bs-agate, d-tv__list/show/body/episodes and tv-poster rules,
which nothing else uses. Phones are unchanged (PhoneTimeline).

Browser checks: home-columns, home-masthead and episode-spacing updated
for the new markup.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BeSUhVSrEYFW7YxEsPgtnC
